# {{pascalCase project.name}} — Architecture

This document is written for two audiences at once: developers and AI coding
agents. It describes how the workspace is organized, how the layers depend on
each other, and which rules generated code follows. Agents must treat the rules
in [.ai/rules/](.ai/README.md) as binding.

## Workspace layout

```text
{{kebabCase project.name}}/
  {{kebabCase project.name}}-backend/    Spring Boot REST API{{#if project.options.frontend}}
  {{kebabCase project.name}}-ui/         Angular single-page application{{/if}}
  entities/         Entity descriptors (YAML) used by the generator
  .ai/              Architecture and naming rules for agents
  .cleanstack/      Generator metadata (do not edit by hand)
  ARCHITECTURE.md   This file
  AGENTS.md         Entry point for AI coding agents
```

## Sides

### Backend — `{{kebabCase project.name}}-backend`

Spring Boot with a layered package structure under
`src/main/java/{{packagePath project.packageName}}`:

| Package | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `domain` | JPA entities and domain models |
| `service` | Use cases and application services |
| `repository` | Spring Data repositories |
| `controller` | REST controllers (`/api/...`) |
| `web.dto` | Request and response types |
| `web.mapper` | HTTP-to-domain mapping |
| `exception` | Exceptions and HTTP status mapping |
| `config`, `security` | Infrastructure configuration |

Details: [{{kebabCase project.name}}-backend/ARCHITECTURE.md]({{kebabCase project.name}}-backend/ARCHITECTURE.md).

{{#if project.options.frontend}}
### Frontend — `{{kebabCase project.name}}-ui`

Angular (standalone components, signals) with a page-first structure under
`src/app`:

| Folder | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `pages/<route>/` | One folder per entity route with `list`, `detail`, and `form` pages |
| `services/` | One HTTP service per entity (`providedIn: 'root'`) |
| `models/` | API types: `<entity>.ts` with an interface and an input type |
| `core/auth/` | Authentication service, guard, and interceptor |
| `layout/`, `shared/`, `api/generated/` | Shell, reusable pieces, generated API client |

The frontend talks to the backend through the `/api` proxy configured in
`src/proxy.conf.json` during development.

{{/if}}
## Request flow

{{#if project.options.frontend}}1. A page component calls an Angular service method
   (`services/<entity>.service.ts`), which sends an HTTP request to
   `/api/<route>` on the backend.
2. A controller validates a request DTO from `web.dto`.
3. A mapper converts the DTO to a domain entity.
4. A service in `service/` applies the use case and calls a repository.
5. The response travels back as a response DTO and is rendered with signals.
{{else}}1. A client sends an HTTP request to `/api/<route>` on the backend.
2. A controller validates a request DTO from `web.dto`.
3. A mapper converts the DTO to a domain entity.
4. A service in `service/` applies the use case and calls a repository.
5. The response travels back as a response DTO.
{{/if}}

## Schema changes

Schema changes are generated from entity descriptors, never written by hand:
{{#if (eq project.options.migrationTool "liquibase")}}
Liquibase changelogs live in
`{{kebabCase project.name}}-backend/src/main/resources/db/changelog/changes`.
{{else}}
Flyway migrations live in
`{{kebabCase project.name}}-backend/src/main/resources/db/migration`.
{{/if}}

Descriptors live in `entities/` (and in `.cleanstack/project.json` metadata);
add or change an entity there, then run `cleanstack entity <Name>` or
`cleanstack regenerate`.

## Rules for agents and humans

1. Follow the layer tables above; dependencies point from controllers/pages
   toward the domain, never the other way around.
2. Name every artifact exactly as described in
   [.ai/rules/naming-conventions.md](.ai/rules/naming-conventions.md).
3. Never edit generated code outside `cleanstack:user-code` regions; see
   [.ai/rules/protected-regions.md](.ai/rules/protected-regions.md).
4. Generate entities with the CLI instead of writing CRUD code by hand; see
   [.ai/rules/adding-an-entity.md](.ai/rules/adding-an-entity.md).

